<h2>Beginner — 9 Habits That Save Context</h2>

<p>The first step to using Claude Code well is not a fancy feature but <strong>the habit of conserving context</strong>. Context is the total amount of conversation and code the model can hold at once; when it fills up, Claude starts forgetting what you agreed on earlier and giving odd answers. This document takes the beginner nine out of a public tutorial's 28 tips and checks each one against Anthropic's official documentation. Every tip links to the official page, so follow the links when you want to go deeper.</p>

